         Question
In the daily standup, it was noted that the timezone settings across the Nautilus Application Servers in the Stratos Datacenter are inconsistent with the local datacenter's timezone, currently set to America/Argentina/San_Luis.
1-Synchronize the timezone settings to match the local datacenter's timezone (America/Argentina/San_Luis).

          Solution
1-Login into each app server and tap the followin command
   ssh user@hostip
 -Verify Current Timezone
 On each App server, check the current timezone:
   timedatectl
 -Set Timezone to America/Argentina/San_Luis
 Run the following command on each App server:
   sudo timedatectl set-timezone America/Argentina/San_Luis
 -Confirm Change
Verify the new timezone setting:
  timedatectl
 You should see:
  Time zone: America/Argentina/San_Luis
      Apply it on each app server
